<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gatsi Rusere</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1589–<a href="/years/1623">1623</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gatsi Rusere was a ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa</a> kingdom from about 1589 to 1623. Faced with rebellions and invasions, he relied more and more on Portuguese military help, and in 1607 he signed a treaty ceding to Portugal the gold, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>, iron, lead and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a> mines of his kingdom in return for support. His reign began the kingdom's slide into dependence on Portugal.</p></div>
